                 1993 vs 2026  ·  a real-time path tracing demo

                   CODE: JOJO · MUSIC: JOYOLO · CONCEPT: JOHN

 --[ RELEASE ]-----------------------------------------------------------------
   Name ......... EVOLUTION
   Type ......... demo, real time, 31 chapters in three acts
   Length ....... 11:51, three tracks by joyolo
   Platforms .... Windows 10/11 x64, Linux x86-64

 --[ SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS ]-----------------------------------------------------
   A Vulkan 1.3 GPU with hardware ray tracing (VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline,
   VK_KHR_ray_query, VK_KHR_acceleration_structure) and about 5 GB of video
   memory. Written for an RTX 4090 at 2560x1440; a slower card runs the same
   show at a lower --trace-scale. A sound device is nice to have; without one
   the demo keeps time on its own.

 --[ RUN ]---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Evolution.exe (or ./Evolution), F11 for full screen. Esc quits.
   Left/Right and 1-0 jump between chapters, C toggles the CRT, H the cards,
   M mutes. --help lists the rest, including the video export.

 --[ GREETINGS ]---------------------------------------------------------------
   FUTURE CREW · TRITON · THE BLACK LOTUS · FARBRAUSCH · CONSPIRACY · ASD
   MERCURY · FAIRLIGHT · HAUJOBB · LOGICOMA · CTRL-ALT-TEST · ANDROMEDA
   MELON DEZIGN · SPACEBALLS · KEWLERS · MFX · STILL · ORANGE · ELUDE
   COCOON · ALCATRAZ · APPROXIMATE

 --[ NOTES ]-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sixty frames a second, eleven minutes, every frame a function of time alone.
Two eras share every frame: a 320x200 screen in 256 colours, and a path tracer.
All numbers on the cards come from the code that draws them; none were typed.
Remainders say what a number leaves the year we live in. Count from A = 1.
 (The music keeps the clock. Without a sound device the demo keeps its own.)
If your GPU is slower than ours, --trace-scale 0.5 still holds every beat.
Thank you for reading the NFO. Almost nobody does.

